WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.690
{only on screen: Kyouko, when we went to the convenience store, you told me the death god costume is embarrassing and I should stop wearing it.}

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.770
taian biyori tenki ga ii nara kimi to

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.770
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
shigoto arimasu you ni ii koto arimasu you ni

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
I hope we have a good time together.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
kyou mo shan shan shan issho ni

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
Today let's keep

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.270
shan shan shan waraou

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.270
Sharing laughs

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.720
hontou no onegaigoto wa kossori kiipu shite kureru

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.720
You keep my true desires secret

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.070
tsuitenai na tte hi no ato wa umeawase shite kureru ne

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.070
You always cheer me up on bad days

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:40.580
chiccha na koro kara kitto minna shitteru

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:40.580
I'm sure everyone has known it since childhood

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
sokkenai furi shinagara itsudemo tsuyoi mikata

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
You pretend you don't care, but you're always a good friend

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:57.480
kamisama wa kyou mo taihen hottokenai shoubu

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:57.480
You have another busy day as a god, with fights you must continue

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:04.990
oisogashii ai de minna no genki wo sotto hitonade

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:04.990
Everyone is cheered up by your radiant glowing love

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.150
kamisama to itsumo issho ni yukai ni naru otetsudai

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.150
You're always with me; helping you is enjoyable.

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:20.820
daiji na egao mamorou kokoroatari aru deshou

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:20.820
I'll protect that precious smile. You know what I mean

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.620
taian biyori tenki ga ii nara kimi to

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.620
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.400
shan shan bouken tokidoki ikanakucha

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.400
We sometimes have to depart on an adventure

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.500
Yaoyorozu-dou

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.660
I wonder what it is.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.340
This is Yaoyorozu-dou, right?

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.380
Sign here, please.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.000
Sure.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:52.710
Um, where's the package?

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.210
Oh, right here.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.710
Mayu-sama, Mayu-sama, please come over here!

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:03.800
What is this?

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.490
Wow, they actually deliver packages this big?

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.500
Oh, reduced regulations...

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:10.810
Now isn't the time to be in awe!

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.060
Well, I mean...

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.190
Yuzu, you said we were flat broke. What did you buy?

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.560
This isn't <i>for me</i>! This is addressed to you, Mayu-sama!

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.950
The sender is...

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.950
Um, I can't really read it.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.280
That is something important.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.610
Handle it with care.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:40.160
Cherry Blossom Front Overture

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.260
What should we do?

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.680
Well, it's not like we can just send it back.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.630
Let's open it first.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:51.390
I'm so excited to see what's inside!

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:52.890
Fragile?

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.090
Fragile

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.890
Feline Triple Front-Flip Attack!

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:56.790
Softly

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.430
It says fragile.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:05.650
Yuzu, I wish you would've pointed that out earlier.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.910
It looks all right though.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.480
Now, what is this?

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.410
A pot?

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:12.830
It's a pot.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.540
Well, that's boring! I guess shouldn't have expected much.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:19.790
Since Shamo-san's gone, I can finally play some games—

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:23.200
Mayu-sama, we can't just leave this huge pot lying here.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.940
Why don't you sell it as an antique item?

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:28.010
No one will buy a pot this huge!

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:28.250
Price: 10,000 yen

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:31.840
This should work; let's wait and see.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.520
Okay...

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.190
Someone will come buy it sooner or later.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.440
Okay...

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.070
What is it this time?

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:54.910
I-I'm sorry! We'll get rid of this by tomorrow!

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.450
I guess that's all right then.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:57.400
Tomorrow's fine for you?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.810
Uh, Yuzu-san,

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.270
wasn't dinner supposed to be egg bowl?

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:07.010
Oh, is that not enough for dinner?

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:06.950
Bottle of
__________dried sardines

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:06.950
dines

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:06.990
Bam

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:06.990
Bottle of
__________dried sardines

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.690
Feel free to help yourself to seconds.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:09.700
Rub

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:15.660
Um, is this because the pot didn't sell today?

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:16.950
No, <i>of course</i> not.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.120
I see.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:22.710
In fact, thanks to that pot, not a single
customer could enter the store today;

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.250
resulting in the lowest amount of customers ever!

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:26.090
Depressed

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.600
Mike

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.260
Oh, Mike!

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.760
Enjoy the food!

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:36.010
He's just a normal cat! How dare he ignore a cat god?!

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:37.180
What?

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.610
I'm sorry!

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:45.350
We have to do something about that pot tomorrow, or it'll become a nuisance for our neighbors.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.140
What should we do?

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:59.310
I can't even imagine what she'll serve
for dinner tomorrow if this continues.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.700
I have no choice.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.090
I'll stealthily dump it somewhere!

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:07.060
Illegal _____dumping

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.950
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.520
Shud

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.210
This is heavy!

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:17.210
What on earth is inside this pot?!

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:20.960
There!

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:23.190
Perfect.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:35.830
Gonta-san, thank you for always sharing with us!

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:39.330
I'll make miso soup for breakfast and use it right away!

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:42.550
Oh, you don't have to do that.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:46.650
Yuzu-san looks so beautiful in an apron!

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.620
She's always in an apron, you know.

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:52.470
Gonta-san, please have breakfast with us before you go.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.180
Oh, can I? Thank you!

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:58.880
Yuzu-san's home cooking!

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.480
Well that's odd,

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:08.800
the cherry blossoms are late to bloom this year.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:09.960
Yeah.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:13.090
They would usually be in full bloom by now.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.490
You're right.

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:19.410
Hmm, bloom prediction for cherry blossoms misses again.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:19.370
Bloom prediction for cherry
blossoms misses again

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:22.220
It's another peaceful day!

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:25.170
Good morning!

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:27.910
Mayu-sama, long time no see!

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.930
Oh, Yoshino, the Cherry Blossom Goddess!

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:34.650
What's going on? How's your grandfather doing?

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:37.180
His chronic lower back pain has gotten worse;

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:40.060
Snap

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.890
so he's staying in bed.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:42.730
That's why I'm here in his place!

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:48.730
So yeah, wasn't a big pot delivered here the other day?

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:49.610
Shock!

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:48.820
Shock

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.730
That's the blooming pot.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:55.030
You mean for cherry blossoms?

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:56.420
Yes, exactly.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:07:04.130
I kinda messed up and sent you the blooming pot instead of Grandpa's cherry blossom pickles that I wanted to share.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.630
These are the pickles I should've sent.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:11.630
How could you possibly have mixed those two up?!

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:16.140
I'm sorry; but that means you received the pot, right?

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:17.140
Thump!

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:16.350
Thump

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:19.050
Yes, I did.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.890
I'm so relieved. Where's the pot?

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:24.400
Oh, <i>that</i> pot?

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:27.300
Mhm, I'm sorry for all the trouble.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.820
So, where is it?

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:31.130
Yes?

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.160
Yes? Yes? Yes? Yes? Yes?

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.120
I threw it away.

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:44.490
Y-You threw it away?!

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.900
Going pale

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.920
Gosh, Mayu, you're so helpless.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.560
So that was Yoshino-san's pot!

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:10.630
I can't believe you threw it away.

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:18.240
You do have a replacement pot, right? Right? Right?

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:22.080
Yes, the pot isn't the problem.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.330
I see; that's great.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:27.300
No, it's not!

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.250
The contents are important!

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:31.780
The contents? What's inside?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:37.220
There are bloom ashes inside.
They take a whole year to make.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:41.700
That is something important.

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:47.830
What's more, only grandpa can make them.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:50.270
Without them, without them...

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:52.760
What happens then?

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.990
I can't make the cherry blossoms bloom this year!

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:57.030
What?!

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:59.030
Stare.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:08:59.080
Thump

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:04.710
Tap

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:06.660
Yoshino!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:12.400
Don't worry; I know exactly where I dumped it!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.670
Everything will be fine if we go pick it up right now.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.630
Really?

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:18.900
You sure it's all right?

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.300
Sh-Shut up!

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:24.600
If you're that worried about it, come with us!

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:29.030
Hmph, you could've just said you needed my help.

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:33.960
Regardless, let's go find that pot as quickly as possible!

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:34.610
Of course!

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:45.120
I think it was around here.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:47.120
You'd better be sure!

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.930
All right! All right!

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:54.080
Okay.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:56.130
Whoa, hey!

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:59.130
Wasn't there a huge pot sitting here?

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:00.710
A pot?

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:05.890
Just so you know, this isn't a garbage dump.

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:08.480
Mayu-sama...

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:09.980
You dumped the pot here?

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:11.930
S-Sorry.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:16.650
So, where's the pot now?

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:20.780
We sent it over to the <i>real</i> landfill!

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:24.910
Illegal dumping of industrial waste is such a pain to deal with.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:28.460
I wish a god would do something about it.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:33.840
Actually, I was the CEO of a corrupt business and making easy money until a few days ago.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:35.840
However, as if by some divine punishment,

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.420
my company went bankrupt.

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:44.210
Albeit, I'm actually glad it fell under. It
made me turn over a new leaf, so to speak.

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:46.960
I've decided to dedicate my life to repaying all the kind—

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:47.850
Huh?

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:49.930
President, is this good enough?

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:53.440
Yes, but I no longer hold that title.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.290
Wh-What should I do?

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:57.820
No, don't cry!

00:10:57.820 --> 00:10:59.470
Mayu, remember this is your fault!

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.960
Don't give up, Yoshino.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.450
Y-Yes.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:05.950
I promise I'll find it.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.990
I would've liked to ride the other train.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:22.580
Thank you, Gonta-san!

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:24.160
You're very welcome!

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:27.720
This must be the landfill.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.600
Good luck finding it as you promised.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:37.480
Your divine powers were taken away because of your mischief.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:42.470
I wonder if you'll still be able to find the pot that easily.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:45.620
She'll be fine.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:50.610
It might have been impossible to find the pot of pickles,

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:53.160
but the other pot was humongous!

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:55.250
Bam

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:02.380
Yeah, the other pot might be big,

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.930
but this place is also quite large.

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:10.010
That's why I'm here!

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:11.270
I'm here for Mayu-sama!

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:12.890
You two again!

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.650
Why is Sasana here?

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:18.650
I could ask <i>you</i> the same thing.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:20.400
I'm having déjà vu here.

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:25.100
I wish you would stop interfering with my business!

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:26.910
Frankly speaking, you're always in the way!

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:29.240
Are you talking about yourself?

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:33.160
Oh, then why don't we see who can find the pot first?

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.290
I accept your challenge.

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:39.130
How about the loser gives up Mayu for good?

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:43.050
Sounds good since I'll be the winner.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.670
You sound so confident!

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:47.430
Stop this!

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:51.680
Please, both of you, help us find the pot.

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:53.900
You can fight afterward.

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:54.680
Okay.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:59.950
I understand; now that that's settled, I'm going to find it!

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:01.690
Meiko, wait!

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:03.650
I can't find it!

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:04.990
Did it get buried?

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:06.730
It should be here!

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:07.700
There! There! There!

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:10.320
It's here! It's here! It's here!

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:13.580
You won't find it over there.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.580
M-Meiko!

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:17.870
Here!

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:19.920
Here! Here! Here! Here!

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:23.710
Cut it out!

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:29.550
You're going to break the pot!

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:35.200
Is everyone all right?

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:37.330
Yeah, sort of.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.750
Those guys!

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:41.190
Huh, Yoshino-san?

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:43.760
I knew it was impossible.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.100
We'll never find it in this huge pile of trash.

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:50.240
I'm sure it's already buried beneath all this garbage.

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:51.990
Yoshino...

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:57.190
This was the first big task Grandpa gave me

00:13:57.190 --> 00:14:00.820
and I lost the precious bloom ashes!

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:02.520
This is hopeless!

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:08.180
If I can't find the pot and make the cherry blossoms bloom,

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.260
everyone will be disappointed.

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:16.520
Yoshino-chan, don't cry.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.550
Don't cry!

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:27.360
Yoshino, perhaps it's too early to give up.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:32.460
Your pot has sensed your presence and is calling out to you.

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:34.870
Can you hear it, Mayu-sama?

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:39.120
Come on, did you forget what kind of god I am?

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:47.820
I am a cat god: a guardian of forgotten items and memories.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.520
Hark, oh bloom pot, thine master commands ye!

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:52.300
Reveal to me your location!

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:09.730
I'm here, Yoshino-chan!

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:14.580
Mayu-sama!

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:15.790
Mayu!

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:21.540
Yoshino?

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.830
I can sense a flower!

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:29.990
This is...!

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.540
There are cracks all over the pot.

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:34.250
It's about to break apart!

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:37.950
It's because you wielded Mekajiki too violently, Sasana!

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:39.880
Meiko, you weren't any better yourself!

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:43.630
Stop it, you two; now is not the time to be bickering.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:45.440
That's right.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:49.540
It looks like this will hold up for now!

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:53.670
How about this?!

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.840
Us too!

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.190
Awesome, this way you can use it again next year!

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:26.700
Thank you so much!

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.550
Thank goodness!

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.450
Still, let's hurry!

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:31.180
Yes!

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:42.230
Oh bloom pot, I apologize profusely
for not assimilating your raison d'être.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.400
For now, I beg thee, bestow upon Yoshino your powers.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:49.690
Mayu-sama!

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:55.490
Mayu-sama, I think we're ready.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:56.770
Yup!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.960
We'll cover the entire Kanto region all at once!

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:00.960
All right!

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.710
Let the withered trees revive,

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:09.470
and the flowers bloom!

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:45.390
Fukushima

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:45.390
Electric Company

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:45.130
The cherry blossoms are blooming everywhere in Kanto.

00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:47.380
That's good.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:50.490
Are you hungry?

00:17:50.490 --> 00:17:51.580
Now that you mention it—

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:53.840
We haven't had breakfast yet.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:58.690
Yoshino-san gave us some cherry blossom pickles. Would you all like to join us?

00:17:58.690 --> 00:17:59.890
Sure!

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:02.810
Mayu-sama.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:03.900
What is it?

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:06.300
Thank you very much.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:09.150
No, I don't deserve your thanks.

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:17.150
After all, I'm the one who screwed up
and threw away your precious pot.

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:22.480
Still, without you, I would've given up long ago.

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:27.030
Unlike you, I still have a long way to go.

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:27.920
Yoshino...

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:34.810
Well actually, I got into so much trouble I was stripped of my divine powers and banished from Heaven.

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:39.610
I'm here on Earth for punishment, so I can't really do much.

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:42.780
You're still amazing though, Mayu-sama!

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:46.370
Don't flatter me too much.
I get easily carried away!

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:48.980
I'm telling the truth!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.540
Oh, really?

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:57.410
There's congestion for one and a half miles at Kawaguchi
Junction, on the Touhoku Expressway, headed toward Tokyo.

00:18:57.410 --> 00:19:01.710
Also for one mile at Misato Junction, on the Jouban Expressway, headed toward Tokyo.

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:08.060
Next, though the cherry blossoms hadn't bloomed yet as predicted by the JMA,

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:14.880
a rare phenomenon occurred this morning when they suddenly all bloomed at the same time; as if to make up for the delay.

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:19.040
Ah, with the cherry blossoms in bloom, it's time to turn over a new leaf and start new work!

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.400
I wish I could watch the flowers bloom this year.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:25.740
Yeah, I haven't seen that in a long time.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:29.710
Yeah, I know! You were always about money-this and money-that.

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:30.530
Huh?!

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:32.120
What's the matter?

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:35.620
This is...!

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:38.230
We got to see them bloom after all.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:39.630
Yeah!

00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:58.110
It's so pretty!

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:00.260
Yuzu-san's so pretty!

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.540
Why are you blushing?

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:04.390
Oh yeah, what happened to your hair?

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:04.240
Collateral damage

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:04.240
1 person

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:05.240
Don't ask.

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:09.490
Have you ever drawn "great curse" as New Year's first omikuji?

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:09.490
TL Note: Omikuji is the tradition of drawing fortunes by giving a small donation at the shrine.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:15.670
I've always believed there isn't a "great curse" omikuji on New Year's Day,

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:15.670
TL Note Cont.: The magnitude of the fortune varies from "great blessing" (highest) to "great curse" (lowest).

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:19.050
Great Curse

00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:19.000
but it seems I may have been mistaken.

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:22.250
On the day of the entrance exam to the school of my dreams,

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:24.910
I was hospitalized after catching the flu.

00:20:26.210 --> 00:20:30.010
The construction company did a shoddy job and my parents' house collapsed.

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:37.840
I thought my series of unfortunate events would be over once I moved to Tokyo and started anew.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.270
"So this is the apartment I'll be living in from now on!"

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:45.660
When I opened the door to my new life, I saw a death god eating a boxed lunch from a convenience store.

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:46.780
"I feel lazy."

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:52.030
So, how long are you going to camp out in my room?

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:55.110
That's not a very nice thing to say.

00:20:55.110 --> 00:21:01.540
It's written in the death god code that death gods can live in room 4 of any apartment.

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:04.530
But you're not paying the rent!

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:10.100
Curry Ramen

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:09.380
Why did I feel a pang in my heart just now?

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:15.650
Hmph! I bet you felt the pang because that manga character loafs
around all day without paying the rent, just like you do. Didn't you?

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:16.740
Didn't you?

00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:17.870
Shut up!

00:21:17.870 --> 00:21:21.310
Jeez, Yuzu-san isn't your wife, Mayu!

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:25.820
Oh? Are you trying to say Mayu is <i>your</i> wife?

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:28.870
I didn't say that!

00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:32.270
You didn't have to say it; it's written all over your face!

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:36.860
Shamo-san, you're here?

00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:39.160
You must really like that game.

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:40.290
What a loafer.

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:41.650
Who are you calling a loafer?

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:42.830
She heard it!

00:21:42.830 --> 00:21:46.230
Actually, I'm here to ask you a favor.

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:46.970
Oh?

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:48.590
It's about none other than...

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:51.040
that manga right there.

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:55.770
Great Curse-chan and
the Happy World

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:55.770
Kamo Yukina

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:09.190
yukkuri nozokikonda ashita to iu mirai

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:09.190
I gently peered into the future which we call tomorrow

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:13.290
sakasama ni nagameta sekai

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:13.290
Looking at the world upside down

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:20.350
kirameku watagashigumo ni omoide wo utsushite

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:20.350
I projected my memories upon the glittering cotton candy clouds

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.460
nanairo no ribon wo kaketa

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.460
And hung rainbow ribbons

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:31.780
hitori ni naru to samishikute fukigen yo

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:31.780
When I'm left alone, I feel lonely and depressed

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:38.250
itsudatte koko ni ite

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:38.250
So stay here forever

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:43.490
dare ni demo kitto aru wa

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:43.490
I'm sure everyone has some

00:22:43.490 --> 00:22:49.400
tojikometa negai no kakera

00:22:43.490 --> 00:22:49.400
Unfulfilled desires locked inside their hearts

00:22:49.400 --> 00:22:51.660
Baby! Oh My God!

00:22:51.660 --> 00:23:01.610
kienai chiisana omoi no kagi ni furete hoshii yeah

00:22:51.660 --> 00:23:01.610
I want you to realize the key is that small memory that won't disappear. Yeah

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:08.080
yasashii kioku e to tsuredaseru no wa

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:08.080
You're always the only one

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:12.370
itsudatte kimi dake

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:12.370
Who can make me reminisce fondly

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:13.940
Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:14.810
Hey Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:14.380 --> 00:23:16.590
Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:15.970 --> 00:23:17.520
Hey Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:19.300
Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:20.380
Hey Baby! Oh My God!

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:41.330
Next Episode

00:23:26.690 --> 00:23:27.900
Ohoho

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:30.610
Yuzu, I have pointy hair!

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:28.740
Whack

00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:32.360
Yes, you sure do.

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:31.280
Five days until the deadline!

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:35.930
I think I'll talk about it in detail next time!

00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:34.120
Weep weep

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:37.230
Oh, in detail?

00:23:37.230 --> 00:23:40.250
No, we'll be drawing manga together!

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:41.330
Deadline Desperation
